1
00:00:00,091 --> 00:00:01,263
Here is the hinge.

2
00:00:01,680 --> 00:00:04,310
In the US, Rana was tried for one specific

3
00:00:04,323 --> 00:00:06,719
crime connected to Mumbai — and acquitted.

4
00:00:07,122 --> 00:00:09,115
But India's charges were different.

5
00:00:09,492 --> 00:00:09,999
Murder.

6
00:00:10,417 --> 00:00:12,331
Waging war against the state.

7
00:00:12,721 --> 00:00:14,635
Terrorism under Indian law.

8
00:00:15,889 --> 00:00:16,814
Same events.

9
00:00:17,204 --> 00:00:18,259
Different crimes.

10
00:00:19,447 --> 00:00:22,260
India had issued a warrant in 2018.

11
00:00:22,650 --> 00:00:24,135
Then came an odd twist.

12
00:00:24,551 --> 00:00:27,754
In 2020, Rana was released early from a US

13
00:00:27,767 --> 00:00:29,786
federal prison on COVID grounds.

14
00:00:31,058 --> 00:00:32,334
He was free for days.

15
00:00:32,751 --> 00:00:35,290
He was re-arrested — this time on India's

16
00:00:35,303 --> 00:00:36,540
extradition request,

17
00:00:36,996 --> 00:00:38,532
filed formally that June.

18
00:00:38,949 --> 00:00:41,306
Rana fought it for nearly five years.

19
00:00:41,696 --> 00:00:44,313
A magistrate certified the extradition.

20
00:00:44,690 --> 00:00:46,487
An appeals court upheld it.

21
00:00:46,891 --> 00:00:48,233
He took it all the way to the

22
00:00:48,246 --> 00:00:49,235
Supreme Court.

23
00:00:49,665 --> 00:00:51,865
His last argument was that he would face

24
00:00:51,878 --> 00:00:54,574
torture in India, in breach of the UN

25
00:00:54,587 --> 00:00:56,019
Convention Against Torture.

26
00:00:57,271 --> 00:00:58,209
It didn't work.

27
00:00:59,870 --> 00:01:02,123
The Ninth Circuit had already answered the

28
00:01:02,136 --> 00:01:02,982
core question.

29
00:01:03,386 --> 00:01:04,909
The crimes charged in India,

30
00:01:05,495 --> 00:01:06,211
the court wrote,

31
00:01:06,667 --> 00:01:09,219
have "elements independent" from those he

32
00:01:09,232 --> 00:01:10,521
had faced in America.

33
00:01:11,808 --> 00:01:14,660
Justice Elena Kagan turned down his final

34
00:01:14,673 --> 00:01:17,720
emergency application in March 2025.

35
00:01:18,110 --> 00:01:20,519
In April, the Court dismissed his last

36
00:01:20,532 --> 00:01:21,131
petition.

37
00:01:22,398 --> 00:01:23,882
No appeals were left.

38
00:01:24,273 --> 00:01:24,898
Not one.

